course: dictionary
lesson: 3857
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and fowl is one of them. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means.
explain: On a farm, fowl are birds kept for their eggs and meat, such as chickens, ducks, geese and turkeys. In «The stew is made of partridges, pheasants, chickens, hares, rabbits, pea-hens, guinea-fowls», the fowl are birds you could cook, so this meaning fits.
explain: The older meaning is any bird. You may meet it in the Bible or in old stories, as in «the fowl of the air». In the phrase «neither fish nor fowl», it means something that is not clearly one thing or another.
fact: Fowl is a noun. You can write a fowl, fowl or fowls.
fact: «Fowl» can mean a bird kept for its eggs or meat, such as a chicken, duck, goose or turkey.
fact: «Wildfowl» are wild ducks and geese.
fact: «Neither fish nor fowl» means not clearly one thing or another.
fact: If the sentence is about eggs, meat or a farm, the first meaning is likely. If it is about old texts, it may mean any bird.
exercise: What does fowl mean in «guinea-fowls» in the stew sentence? | Small furry animals | Trees with long roots | Fish caught in a river | *Birds kept for eggs or meat
exercise: What are wildfowl? | Fish that live in rock pools | *Wild ducks and geese | Wild cats that hunt mice | Tall grass by a lake
exercise: What does «neither fish nor fowl» mean? | *Not clearly one thing or another | Clearly a fish | Something very loud | A very large bird
test: In the old phrase «the fowl of the air», what does fowl mean? | A goose at the seaside | A chicken kept on a farm | *Any bird | A fish
test: Which word means birds kept on a farm for eggs and meat? | fox | *fowl | fern | fudge
exam: Jayden reads «The lake was full of wildfowl, ducks and geese swimming in the reeds.» What does wildfowl mean? | *Wild ducks and geese | Flowers | Wild cats | Fish
